# command: DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_URL=https://<node>:8006 DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_NODE=pve DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_USER=root@pam DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_PASS=… DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_BACKUP_STORAGE=local DELONIX_PROXMOX_TRACE_ROUTES=docs/proxmox/trace-9.2.2.routes cargo test -p delonix-proxmox --test live -- --nocapture --test-threads=1
# result: 8 passed (o_ip_vem_do_agente_de_um_convidado_a_serio skipped: no DELONIX_PROXMOX_TEST_AGENT_VMID); the lifecycle case walks create → snapshot (RAM) → rollback → delete-snapshot → stop → resume → stop → destroy; the template case makes its own template, grows it, refuses a shrink clone, clones it at two sizes, destroys the clones and the template; the backup case backs up a running VM twice, lists the archives, deletes both, and confirms an unknown volid is refused; the restore case backs up a VM, destroys it, restores the archive into the vacated vmid, confirms the restored boot disk matches the original size, confirms restoring over an occupied vmid is refused; the agent case pings a guest with no agent (Ok(false), never an Err); the firewall case enables the VM's own native firewall, adds a rule, reads it back, updates it, deletes it and confirms the node's list is empty, then disables the firewall again; the node registers the workers as `qmcreate`/`qmstart`/`qmstop`/`qmsnapshot`/`qmrollback`/`qmdelsnapshot`/`qmdestroy`/`qmconfig`/`qmclone`/`qmtemplate`/`resize`/`vzdump`/`imgdel`/`qmrestore` — `agent/ping` and every per-VM firewall write fork no task at all (apply inline)
